=== HINT 1 ===
On x64:  PPEB peb = (PPEB)__readgsqword(0x60);
On x86:  PPEB peb = (PPEB)__readfsdword(0x30);

=== HINT 2 ===
PLIST_ENTRY head = &peb->Ldr->InMemoryOrderModuleList;
PLIST_ENTRY cur  = head->Flink;


LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY is 2 LIST_ENTRYs into the structure when using
InMemoryOrderModuleList.  Use CONTAINING_RECORD:
  PLDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY entry = CONTAINING_RECORD(
      cur, LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY, InMemoryOrderLinks);

entry->BaseDllName.Buffer is a WCHAR*.
Use _wcsicmp(entry->BaseDllName.Buffer, name_w) == 0 for case-insensitive match.
Return (HMODULE)entry->DllBase on match.
Stop when cur == head (full circle).

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
PPEB peb = (PPEB)__readgsqword(0x60);
PLIST_ENTRY head = &peb->Ldr->InMemoryOrderModuleList;
PLIST_ENTRY cur  = head->Flink;
while (cur != head) {
    PLDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY e = CONTAINING_RECORD(cur, LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY, InMemoryOrderLinks);
    if (e->BaseDllName.Buffer && _wcsicmp(e->BaseDllName.Buffer, name_w) == 0)
        return (HMODULE)e->DllBase;
    cur = cur->Flink;
}
return NULL;
